{{- $c := .Local -}}
{{- $cliName := $c.CliName -}}
{{- $retryVisibility := retryFlagsVisibility -}}
Some operations in this CLI support automatic retries with exponential backoff.

{{ if ne $retryVisibility "visible" -}}
### Configure retries

{{ if eq $retryVisibility "hidden" -}}
Retry flags are supported but intentionally omitted from `--help`. For persistent agent configuration, use `~/.config/{{$cliName}}/config.yaml`:
{{ else -}}
Retry flags are not registered. Configure retries in `~/.config/{{$cliName}}/config.yaml`:
{{ end }}
```yaml
timeout: 30s
no_retries: false
retry_connection_errors: true
retry_max_elapsed_time: 1m
# retry_config replaces the whole policy (overrides retry_max_elapsed_time):
# retry_config: '{"strategy":"backoff","backoff":{"initialInterval":500,"maxInterval":60000,"exponent":1.5,"maxElapsedTime":300000}}'
```

{{ if eq $retryVisibility "hidden" -}}
The equivalent hidden flags are `--no-retries`, `--retry-config`, `--retry-connection-errors`, and `--retry-max-elapsed-time`.

{{ end -}}
{{ else -}}
### Retry controls

```bash
# Disable retries for one command
{{$c.Showcase}} --no-retries

# Replace the retry policy with backoff capped by elapsed time
{{$c.Showcase}} --retry-max-elapsed-time 5s

# Retry eligible connection errors
{{$c.Showcase}} --retry-connection-errors

# Supply the complete retry configuration
{{$c.Showcase}} --retry-config '{"strategy":"backoff","backoff":{"initialInterval":500,"maxInterval":60000,"exponent":1.5,"maxElapsedTime":300000}}'
{{ if hasAttemptCountRetries -}}

# Bound retries by attempt count instead
{{$c.Showcase}} --retry-config '{"strategy":"attempt-count-backoff","maxRetries":2,"backoff":{"initialInterval":500,"maxInterval":60000,"exponent":2,"maxElapsedTime":300000}}'
{{ end -}}
```

### Persist retry settings

Add retry configuration with `{{$cliName}} configure` or edit `~/.config/{{$cliName}}/config.yaml`:

```yaml
timeout: 30s
no_retries: false
retry_connection_errors: true
retry_max_elapsed_time: 1m
# retry_config replaces the whole policy (overrides retry_max_elapsed_time):
# retry_config: '{"strategy":"backoff","backoff":{"initialInterval":500,"maxInterval":60000,"exponent":1.5,"maxElapsedTime":300000}}'
```

{{ end -}}
{{ if eq (retryMethodPolicy) "safe-methods" -}}
### Method retry policy

Root-level retry policies apply only to safe HTTP methods: `GET`, `HEAD`, `OPTIONS`, and `TRACE`. An explicit operation-level retry policy may opt another method in. Runtime retry settings cannot enable retries for an operation that has no generated retry loop.

{{ end -}}
### Retry-After

`Retry-After` (integer seconds or an RFC1123 date) and `retry-after-ms` override the next computed interval. With the `backoff` strategy, a server-directed wait that exceeds the remaining `maxElapsedTime` budget is not slept; the last response is returned.{{ if hasAttemptCountRetries }} With `attempt-count-backoff`, `maxRetries` bounds attempts, while `timeout` bounds wall-clock time; `maxElapsedTime` does not apply.{{ end }}

### Timeout

`timeout` and `--timeout` bound the whole operation, including retry sleeps:

```bash
{{$c.Showcase}} --timeout 30s
```

{{ if eq $retryVisibility "none" -}}
**Precedence**: `no_retries` > `retry_config` > `retry_max_elapsed_time`/`retry_connection_errors` > API specification defaults.
{{ else -}}
**Precedence**: `--no-retries` > `--retry-config` > individual flags > config file > API specification defaults.
{{ end }}
